{"diagnosis": "Loopback uart with divider 64 sent 0xa5 but recv returned 0xe0 causing `TRAP: uart data mismatch got 0xe0 want 0xa5` and tohost FAIL 0xdead. Root cause in excerpt is recv bit-period compare uses `(cfg_divider >> 4)` at lines 90 and 97 for data/stop states, sampling ~16x too fast instead of full `cfg_divider`. Via cone picosoc/picosoc.v:190 instance to picosoc/simpleuart.v:20, half-bit align `2*recv_divcnt > cfg_divider` at line 84 is correct, so data bits must use full divider.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -89,14 +89,14 @@
 				10: begin
-					if (recv_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4)) begin
+					if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
 						recv_buf_data <= recv_pattern;
 						recv_buf_valid <= 1;
 						recv_state <= 0;
 					end
 				end
 				default: begin
-					if (recv_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4)) begin
+					if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
 						recv_pattern <= {ser_rx, recv_pattern[7:1]};
 						recv_state <= recv_state + 1;
 						recv_divcnt <= 0;
 					end
 				end
", "expected": "tohost PASS (was FAIL 0xdead), no TRAP, uart loopback 0xa5 matched, checksum != 27ee482b473c74db5dce8b5ab1a233084cce3055c317a1f2045faa6dbc13a1c6"}

